A little walkthrough the situation : 

*Assuming that `<input>` value is `"x"` and you type backspace :*  

- When the `keydown` event fires the input's value is still `"x"`.  

- When the `keypress` fires, it still `"x"`.  

If you **don't** release the key :  

\_\_ `keydown` fires again, after some delay, depending on os I guess value is now `""`.  

\_\_ `keypress` fires again, value is still `""`.  

\_\_ When you release the key, `keyup` fires, value is `""`.  

If you **do** release the key :  

\_\_ `keypress` fires directly, value is `""`.

The solution For IE10+ is to use the [`input`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Events/input) event which will fire when the textEditable element's content has changed or, as suggested by @Mayhem, the [`change`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Events/change) event, which won't even listen for key inputs and has a better browser support than `input`

```js
$('#tbox').on('input change',function(e){
    if($('#tbox').val() !== '') {
        $('#btn').css({'display':'block'});
    } else {
        $('#btn').css({'display':'none'});
    }
});
```

